From e416baf1557cd68201801b27d32eeb47e61ebf14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kykifox1337-source <kykifox1337@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:10:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] d3d12: SYNC_COPY waits for the CLEAR stage too (D3D-838)

An enhanced barrier's D3D12_BARRIER_SYNC_COPY mapped to VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_2_COPY_BIT only. Two D3D12
copy-scope commands are not Vulkan copies: WriteBufferImmediate is recorded as vkCmdUpdateBuffer and
ResolveQueryData's never-written queries as vkCmdFillBuffer, and synchronization2 runs both in the CLEAR
stage. A SYNC_COPY barrier after either therefore did not order it, and a copy after the barrier could read
the word before the write landed.

vulkan_sync now maps SYNC_COPY to COPY | CLEAR. vk_command_replay_test part K records WriteBufferImmediate,
a SYNC_COPY -> SYNC_COPY buffer barrier and a CopyBufferRegion of the written word; under
LEONIDA_VK_VALIDATION=1 it is a read-after-write hazard without this change. d3d12_state_map_test and
docs/d3d12_vulkan.md follow the new mapping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit bbc8999d509422782f39e106a77205b1d4f4dda4)
